Personnel Activation and Sign-In System Roadmap (Supabase Integration)


Phase 1: Supabase Database & Security Setup

 * Step 1: Create the pre_approved_personnel Table
   * Open your Supabase SQL Editor and create the whitelist table to store your pre-approved staff details (initials, firstname, surname, email, phone, role, and temppass).

 * Step 2: Create the personnel Table
   * Create the active personnel table in PostgreSQL to store registered users (id, personnel_number, initials, firstname, surname, email, phone, role, is_active). Set personnel_number to UNIQUE so duplicates are physically impossible at the database level.

 * Step 3: Enable Row Level Security (RLS)
   * Apply RLS policies to both tables so that unauthenticated users cannot read or modify administrative data directly.

 * Step 4: Copy Your Supabase API Keys
   * Go to Project Settings > API in your Supabase dashboard and copy your Project URL and anon public key.


Phase 2: Manual Pre-Approval Data Entry

 * Step 5: Insert Test Pre-Approved Personnel
   * Go to the Table Editor in Supabase, select pre_approved_personnel, and manually insert a test staff record (with your test email, name, role, and temporary password) so you have data to test activation against.


Phase 3: Project File Restructuring

 * Step 6: Create supabase-config.js
   * Delete or replace firebase-config.js with a new supabase-config.js file that initializes the Supabase JS SDK using your Project URL and anon key.

 * Step 7: Update admin-home.html Script References
   * Ensure admin-home.html links to your updated JavaScript files and that field inputs and IDs match the Supabase connection setup.


Phase 4: JavaScript Logic Implementation (admin-home.js)

 * Step 8: Implement Form Field Formatting & Validation
   * Keep your auto-capitalization on blur and live password criteria check (8 to 12 characters, uppercase letter, number, underscore, and matching confirmation).

 * Step 9: Build the Activation Logic (supabase.from('pre_approved_personnel'))
   * On activation submit: query pre_approved_personnel to verify that all entered details match the pre-approved record exactly. Deny access if any field fails to match.

 * Step 10: Build Account Creation & Personnel Number Generation
   * On successful pre-approval match: call supabase.auth.signUp(), generate a random 8-digit MyAtlas Personnel Number, check database uniqueness, and write the permanent record into the personnel table with is_active: false.

 * Step 11: Configure Welcome Email Trigger
   * Trigger an automated email to send the generated 8-digit MyAtlas Personnel Number to the user's email address upon successful activation.

 * Step 12: Build the Sign-In Verification Logic (supabase.auth.signInWithPassword)
   * On sign-in submit: authenticate the email and password via Supabase Auth, then cross-check personnel_number, email, role, and is_active status in the personnel table. Block login if details don't align or if is_active is false.


Phase 5: Testing & Verification

 * Step 13: Test Mismatched Activation
   * Submit incorrect names or temporary passwords to confirm the system rejects unauthorized activation attempts.

 * Step 14: Test Valid Activation & Account Creation
   * Submit valid matching details, verify that the new account appears under Supabase Auth and the personnel table, and confirm the 8-digit personnel number is generated cleanly.

 * Step 15: Test Sign-In & Dashboard Redirect
   * Log in with the new personnel number, email, password, and role to verify successful redirection to admin.html.
